AU  - LAKSHMANAN P
TI  - Active noise cancelation system e.g. e.g. sky            silence for e.g. drone used in e.g. aerial surveillance            domain, has isolated power management circuit            integrated with electromagnetic interference shielding            function used to prevent interference with navigation            and communication systems
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a microphone array with 4-8                micro-electro-mechanical system (MEMS) microphones                positioned on propeller arms to capture rotor noise                in a 100-2000 Hertz frequency range. A digital                signal processor (DSP) unit employs filtered-x                Least mean squares (FxLMS) adaptive algorithm to                generate phase-inverted antinoise signals. Multiple                compact acoustic drivers are mounted near rotors to                emit anti-noise. A flight controller interface                receives real-time revolutions per minute (RPM)                data through a controller area network(CAN) bus or                pulse width modulation (PWM) to synchronize noise                cancellation with propeller rotation cycles. An                isolated power management circuit integrated with                electromagnetic interference (EMI) shielding                function is used to prevent interference with                navigation and communication systems.
                    USE - Active noise cancelation (ANC) system e.g. sky                silence for a military and defense unmanned aerial                vehicle (UAV) e.g. a drone used in various domains                such as aerial surveillance, logistics and                environmental monitoring.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system reduces acoustic signature of an                UAV during tactical operations, thus enhancing                operational stealth and mission effectiveness in                defense applications. The system identifies,                captures and analyzes the dominant acoustic                signatures of military UAVs, including propeller                blade-pass frequency, motor electromagnetic noise,                and airframe vibration, to enable precise                threat-signature characterization and suppression.                The system designs a ruggedized adaptive ANC                architecture employing strategically positioned                microphones and precision acoustic transducers to                generate phase-inverted anti-noise signals that                achieve destructive interference with acoustic                emissions of the UAV. The system develops a                real-time digital signal processing algorithm                optimized for tactical environments, capable of                generating accurate inverse phase signals through                advanced adaptive filtering techniques such as                FxLMS, Recursive Least Squares (RLS), or neural                network-based predictive models. The system                integrates multi-modal sensing including MEMS                accelerometers, piezoelectric vibration sensors,                and distributed acoustic arrays for robust feed                forward and feedback control, thus ensuring                consistent noise suppression across variable flight                regimes, payload configurations, and hostile                environmental conditions. The system achieves                ultra-low latency and minimal power overhead                through implementation of a hardened embedded                processing architecture utilizing FPGA or dedicated                DSP chips, suitable for size, weight, and                power-constrained military UAV platforms. The                system ensures system modularity and rapid                integration compatibility with existing military                UAV airframes through standardized mounting                interfaces and plug-and-play electronic                integration, thus requiring minimal structural or                avionic modifications. The system delivers                measurable acoustic signature reduction to enhance                tactical stealth, reduce detection probability by                adversarial acoustic sensors, enable covert                reconnaissance and surveillance missions, and                provide operational advantages in contested                airspace and proximity operations in urban warfare                environments.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of an ANC                system.
