TI  - Position location and tracking method for e.g.            urban warfare involves generating player position data            in each player unit based on sensor signal that is            output from field sensor to represent magnetic signals            radiating from antennas
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - A transmitter coupled to each of the multiple                antennas produces signal current to radiate a                magnetic signal. Each player unit has a field                sensor to produce a sensor signal representing the                magnetic signals radiating from the antennas, and a                signal processor for generating player position                data, based on the sensor signal.
