TI  - Data-knowledge-driven Metaverse Modeling Framework for UrbanWarfare
T2  - Journal of Command and Control
M3  - Article
AB  - The metaverse gives a new technology for operational modeling due to the feature of deep immersion and the fusion of virtual and reality in it. On this basis, a novel data-knowledge-driven metaverse modeling framework for urban warfare is proposed. Based on this framework, knowledge graphs, generative confrontation networks and other relative theories and methods are applied. The environment ontology modeling problem for urban warfare in metaverse scenario is explored, the improvement example scheme for urban warfare model of metaverse is designed to realize the good performance and super scalability. The relative quantitative experiments and verifications are carried out. The metaverse modeling framework for urban warfare is expected to become a new designed paradigm of intelligent decision-making with combination of virtual and reality.
