TI  - Integrated focal plane sensor array for radiation            sensing equipment in security system, has infrared and            millimeter wave sensors provided on common plane, and            antenna on lower plane
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - An array of infrared (IR) sensors (17) and at                least one millimeter (mm) wave sensor (20) are                provided at a common planar level on a front                surface (21) of a substrate (11). A planar antenna                (15) is located at a lower planar level between the                common planar level and front surface of the                substrate, to couple the mm wave radiation field to                the mm wave sensor.
                    USE - For radiation sensing equipment used in                security standoff systems, airport security                systems, weather landing aids, mine detection,                missile homing, urban warfare, etc.
                    ADVANTAGE - Provides bona fide integrated structure with                the combination of both types of sensors fabricated                upon the same side of the substrate, thus resulting                in much smaller and lower cost system. Provides                same, naturally aligned field of view (FOV) for                both imaging domains and hence simplifies the                sensor fusion algorithms significantly.                Consequently, the need for the high speed, high                power computing is reduced. The integrated sensor                offers manufacturing ease, as only simple                processing and components are required.
