TI  - Ultra-wideband impulse radar-based bird detection            and recognition method for e.g. urban warfare, involves            converting processed echo signals into digital signals,            receiving and processing digital signals, generating            bird recognition result, and transmitting result to            display-control module
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves transmitting (S1) start                operation command to a control module. The start                operation command is received (S2) and trigger                signal is transmitted to an excitation signal                generator. The trigger signal is received (S3) and                pulse width modulation signal is generated. The                pulse width modulation signal is received (S4) and                zero-order Gaussian pulse signal is transmitted to                transmitting antenna array. The zero-order Gaussian                pulse signal is received (S5), and the detection                signal is generated. The echo signals are received                and processed (S6), and the processed echo signals                are transmitted to an analog-to-digital converter                module. The processed echo signals are converted                (S7) into digital signals and transmitted to the                control module. The digital signals are received                and processed (S8), bird recognition result is                generated, and the result is transmitted to the                display-control module. The bird recognition result                is received and displayed (S9).
                    USE - Ultra-wideband impulse radar-based bird                detection and recognition method for short-range                detection scenario such as urban warfare,                geological exploration and biomedical                application.
                    ADVANTAGE - By designing high-power avalanche transistor                Marx circuit as the pulse source for the                ultra-wideband impulse radar, the signal-to-noise                ratio of the echo signal is effectively improved.                By introducing a deep learning model to process the                echo data, the method enhances the system ability                to recognize bird targets with complex reflection                characteristics.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a                ultra-wideband impulse radar-based bird detection                and recognition device.
