TI  - System for deploying wireless mesh sensor array            network by aircraft for real-time environmental data            gathering during e.g. fires, has drop pods provided            with connection interface for aircraft, and pod sensor            module provided with sensors
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) has multiple drop pods (112)                provided with a connection interface for an                aircraft. A pod sensor module is provided with                sensors, where the sensor is provided with cameras,                microphones, gas sensors and temperature sensors.                The drop pods are configured to be retrieved or                repositioned by the aircraft. The connection                interface is provided with an electromagnet. A                first camera is arranged on a first side of the                drop pod. A second camera is arranged on a second                opposite side of the drop pod. A mesh radio module                is configured to create a mesh wireless network                (130) with other drop pods and to create a mesh                wireless network with the aircraft. An aircraft                mesh radio module is communicated with a Ground                Control Station (GCS) (105) and the drop                pods.
                    USE - System for deploying a wireless mesh sensor                array network by an aircraft for real-time                environmental data gathering in a hazardous                environment during dangerous situations e.g. fires,                active shooter scenarios, urban warfare or hostage                situations.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system allows a master mesh radio module                to communicate with the drop pod bay unit over the                mesh network, so that the master radio module can                communicate with a slave radio module over the                master mesh network in an efficient manner. The                system enables the drop pods to be attached to the                aircraft in an effective manner, thus providing                reliable communication and environmental data, and                hence reducing risk of fire and natural disasters                in a cost-effective manner and reducing danger to                responders in search for survivors.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method                for deploying a real-time environmental data                gathering system.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic block diagram                of a system for deploying a wireless mesh sensor                array network by an aircraft for real-time                environmental data gathering in a hazardous                environment during dangerous situations.100Autonomous drone mesh sensor deployment                system105Ground control station110Drones112Drop pods115Datastores130Networks
