TI  - Interactive laser tag system for entertaining e.g.            children to play scene-laser fight games, has global            positioning system for providing locations of players,            where data is made available to players and software            operates on display device
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) has a server (19) for                enabling a login of a player of a game, which                resides on the server. A global positioning system                (GPS) provides locations of the players, where GPS                data is made available to the players and web-based                software operates on a mobile display device (13)                that calculates and determines hit by the player                registered, generates vibration, plays sound and                visual effects of toy laser weapons (10) on the                mobile display device and generates a graphical                user interface displayed on the mobile display                device kept with the players to enhance the effects                of the game.
                    USE - Interactive laser tag system for entertaining                multiple play participants e.g. children and                adults, to play games e.g. scene-laser fight games,                dragon fighting games, urban warfare-sniper games,                ninja fighting games and battlefield gaming                scene-combat fight games (all claimed), in                entertainment/education applications e.g. reading                applications, memory stimulation applications,                tactile coordination applications, children's                imagination stimulation applications and creativity                and social interactivity applications. Can also be                used for soldier games, warrior games, robotic                games, alien games and mythical games.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system defines acceleration, gyroscopic                and magnetic sensors that integrate Bluetooth                technologies with opportunities by a mobile                computing phone to make gaming experience of laser                tag gamers more interesting and challenging in an                effective manner.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - The toy laser weapons are selected from a                group consisting of laser tag swords, spike                weapons, knife weapons, fireball weapons, shield                weapons, glove weapons, spear weapons and bow                weapons. The mobile display devices are selected                from a group consisting of wearable computers,                mobile phones and mini LCDs. An INDEPENDENT CLAIM                is also included for a method for providing an                interactive game.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a perspective view of an                interactive laser tag system.Toy laser weapons (10)Trigger (11)Mobile display devices (13, 17)Server (19)Interactive laser tag system (100)
