T2  - 군사발전연구
M3  - research-article
AB  - The Russo-Ukrainian War, which was sparked by Russia’s invasion of Ukraine on February 24th, 2022, shows various aspects of warfare both in the present and future, along with the rapid changes in the existing international order and world economy.This war is not only a miniature version of all wars of blitzkrieg, air combat, urban warfare, guerrilla warfare, psychological warfare and information warfare that have taken place over the last 100 years, but it is also an example of the complexity of future warfare such as whole-territorial warfare, hybrid warfare, manned and unmanned combined warfare, and non-linear warfare. In particular, the non-linear warfare demonstrated by the attacker, the Russian army, and the defender, the Ukrainian army, demonstrate the future warfare that our army should carry out in the future.The purpose of this study was to analyze the non-linear warfare by the Russian and Ukrainian forces, and thus to explore the direction of improvement of non-linear warfare that the Republic of Korea (ROK) Army should carry out in the future.This paper is a case study on the ongoing war and is presented based on analysis data from related research institutes and press releases due to limitations in collecting primary data and specific cases. However, the study has significance in that it suggests the improvement direction for non-linear warfare that our army should carry out in the future through the understudied topic of non-linear warfare at the private level.The Yoon government is concentrating all its efforts on fostering a strong AI scientific technology force by promoting Defense Innovation 4.0 based on the advanced technology of the Fourth Industrial Revolution such as hyper-connectivity, superintelligence, space, unmanned robots, and new energy. In order to carry out powerful non-linear warfare in a future multi-disciplinary operational environment, the ROK military should continue to secure an intelligent network-oriented operational environment that applies advanced science and technology, contactless precision strikes, and non-linear multidimensional deep maneuver capabilities.
